# CAPA templates (TECH 4, FI 1)

template capa-request | CAPA Request | CAPA
packs medical-device, manufacturing
tags CAPA, request
purpose Request a corrective or preventive action for a problem or risk whose cause must be found and removed, and decide whether a CAPA is warranted.
scope Requests from nonconformances, complaints, audits, process monitoring, risk reviews, management review and any employee.
instructions Describe the problem with data and reference the source records. The CAPA review board screens the request against the organization's criteria and either opens a CAPA, links it to an existing one or rejects it with a reason.
workflow Requested, screened, accepted and assigned or rejected with reason.
retention Keep for ten years after the decision.
status Draft; Submitted; Accepted; Linked to existing CAPA; Rejected
use capa_problem
section screening | Screening | 2
f requested_by | Requested by | user | *
f action_type_requested | Action type | choice | * [Corrective; Preventive]
f screening_criteria | Screening criteria met | multichoice | [Severity; Repeat occurrence; Customer impact; Regulatory impact; Safety; Cost; Trend]
f screening_decision | Decision | choice | [Open CAPA; Link to existing CAPA; Handle as correction only; Reject]
f screening_reason | Reason for decision | longtext | reqwhen=screening_decision~Reject/Handle_as_correction_only
f existing_capa | Existing CAPA | record | when=screening_decision=Link_to_existing_CAPA
f proposed_owner | Proposed owner | user
sign request_signed | Requested by | prepared | I request this action on the information recorded.
sign screening_signed | Screened by | approved | I record the screening decision. | capa.approve
end

template capa-investigation | CAPA Investigation | CAPA
packs medical-device, manufacturing
tags CAPA, investigation
purpose Plan and record the investigation of a CAPA: the team, the data reviewed, the analysis and the verified root cause.
scope All accepted CAPAs.
instructions Assemble a cross-functional team, collect data, analyse causes with a recognized method, and verify the root cause before planning actions. Record data sources so the investigation can be reproduced.
workflow Investigation planned, data collected, analysis complete, root cause verified, reviewed.
retention Keep for ten years after CAPA closure.
use capa_problem, team, capa_root_cause, capa_signatures
section data_review | Data reviewed | 1
table data_sources | Data sources | 1
c data_source | Data source | text | *
c data_period | Period | text
c data_finding | Finding | longtext | *
c data_by | Reviewed by | user
end

template correction-record | Correction Record | CAPA
packs medical-device, manufacturing
tags correction
purpose Record the correction made to eliminate a detected nonconformity, such as rework, replacement or a corrected record, separately from the corrective action that addresses its cause.
scope Corrections linked to nonconformances, audit findings, complaints and CAPAs.
instructions Describe what was corrected, how and by whom, and verify the correction. A correction alone does not prevent recurrence; link a CAPA when the cause needs action.
workflow Recorded, carried out, verified.
retention Keep for ten years after closure.
use ncr_quantity, ncr_verification
section correction_details | Correction | 2
f source_record_ref | Source record | record | *
f correction_description | Correction made | longtext | *
f corrected_by | Corrected by | user | *
f corrected_on | Corrected on | date | *
f cause_action_needed | Corrective action needed | boolean
f capa_link | CAPA | record | when=cause_action_needed=true
use approval_trio
end

template containment-plan | Containment Plan | CAPA
packs medical-device, manufacturing
tags containment, plan
purpose Plan the containment of a problem across every location where suspect product or process output may exist, with owners, dates and exit criteria.
scope Containment for CAPAs, customer complaints and significant nonconformances.
instructions List every location and channel, assign an owner and a date, define how suspect product is checked and how cleared product is identified, and set the criteria for ending containment.
workflow Planned, approved, executed, verified, ended.
retention Keep with the CAPA for ten years after closure.
use ncr_containment
section containment_plan_section | Plan | 2
f suspect_population | Suspect population | longtext | *
f check_method | Check method | longtext | *
f cleared_identification | Cleared product identification | text
f containment_exit | Exit criteria | longtext | *
table containment_tasks | Containment tasks | 1
c task_location | Location | text | *
c task_action | Action | text | *
c task_owner | Owner | user | *
c task_due | Due | date | *
c task_done | Done | boolean
use approval_trio
end

template root-cause-analysis-record | Root Cause Analysis | CAPA
packs medical-device, manufacturing
tags root cause, analysis
purpose Record a structured root cause analysis for a CAPA, nonconformance or complaint, from problem definition through verified root causes.
scope Any investigation that requires a documented root cause.
instructions Define the problem, list candidate causes by category, test each candidate against the evidence, and record which causes are verified. Separate the cause of occurrence from the cause of non-detection.
workflow Problem defined, candidate causes listed, causes tested, root causes verified, reviewed.
retention Keep with the parent record for ten years after closure.
use capa_problem, team, capa_root_cause
section candidate_causes | Candidate causes | 1
table causes | Candidate causes | 1
c cause_category | Category | choice | * [Method; Machine; Material; Measurement; People; Environment; Design; Management system]
c cause_text | Candidate cause | longtext | *
c cause_test | How tested | text
c cause_result | Result | choice | [Verified; Not verified; Contributing; Not tested]
rule causes.cause_result | equals | Verified | #E6F4EA | bold
use approval_trio
end

template corrective-action-plan | Corrective Action Plan | CAPA
packs medical-device, manufacturing
tags corrective action, plan
purpose Plan the actions that remove the verified root causes, with owners, dates, the risk of each change and how implementation and effectiveness will be verified.
scope Corrective actions for accepted CAPAs.
instructions Address each verified root cause with at least one action. Assess whether actions change documents, processes, training or validated states and raise the related changes. Set measurable effectiveness criteria now.
workflow Planned, reviewed, approved, actions in progress, implementation verified.
retention Keep with the CAPA for ten years after closure.
use action_plan, capa_effectiveness, capa_signatures
section plan_impacts | Impact of the actions | 2
f capa_ref | CAPA | record | *
f root_causes_addressed | Root causes addressed | longtext | *
f documents_affected | Documents affected | longtext
f training_needed | Training needed | boolean
f validation_impact | Revalidation needed | boolean
f risk_file_update | Risk assessment update needed | boolean
f change_request_link | Change request | record
end

template preventive-action-plan | Preventive Action Plan | CAPA
packs medical-device, manufacturing
tags preventive action, plan
purpose Plan action against the cause of a potential nonconformity identified from trends, risk assessments or lessons learned elsewhere, before it occurs.
scope Preventive actions arising from data analysis, risk reviews, management review and similar products or processes.
instructions Describe the potential problem and the evidence that it could occur, the cause to be removed, and the actions with owners and dates. Set measurable criteria that show the risk was reduced.
workflow Proposed, reviewed, approved, actions in progress, verified.
retention Keep for ten years after closure.
use action_plan, capa_effectiveness, capa_signatures
section potential_problem | Potential problem | 2
f potential_problem_text | Potential problem | longtext | *
f trigger | Trigger | choice | * [Trend; Risk assessment; Lessons learned; Similar product; Audit observation; Management review; Other]
f evidence_of_risk | Evidence that it could occur | longtext | *
f potential_cause | Cause to be removed | longtext | *
f risk_before | Risk level before | choice | [High; Medium; Low]
f risk_after | Target risk level after | choice | [High; Medium; Low]
end

template implementation-verification | Implementation Verification | CAPA
packs medical-device, manufacturing
tags verification, implementation
purpose Verify that every planned CAPA action was implemented as planned, with objective evidence, before effectiveness is reviewed.
scope All corrective and preventive actions.
instructions For each action, record the evidence of implementation and whether it was implemented as planned. An action not implemented as planned is re-planned before the CAPA proceeds.
workflow Evidence collected, each action verified, verification approved.
retention Keep with the CAPA for ten years after closure.
section implementation | Implementation evidence | 1
f capa_ref | CAPA | record | *
table implementation_checks | Actions verified | 1
c impl_action | Action | text | *
c impl_evidence | Evidence | longtext | *
c impl_as_planned | Implemented as planned | passfail | *
c impl_verified_by | Verified by | user | *
c impl_date | Date | date | *
f actions_total | Actions verified | calc | {COUNTA(implementation_checks.impl_action)}
f actions_failed | Not implemented as planned | calc | {COUNTIF(implementation_checks.impl_as_planned, "FAIL")}
rule implementation_checks.impl_as_planned | equals | FAIL | #FDE7E9 | bold
sign impl_prepared | Verified by | performed | I verified the implementation of the actions listed.
sign impl_approved | Approved by | approved | I accept the implementation verification. | capa.approve
end

template effectiveness-review | Effectiveness Review | CAPA
packs medical-device, manufacturing
tags effectiveness
purpose Decide on objective data whether CAPA actions prevented recurrence and achieved the criteria set when they were planned.
scope All CAPAs after implementation verification.
instructions Collect data for the full monitoring period, compare it with the baseline and the target, check for recurrence and for new problems introduced. A not effective result reopens the investigation.
workflow Monitoring period complete, data reviewed, effectiveness decided, approved.
retention Keep with the CAPA for ten years after closure.
use capa_effectiveness
section recurrence | Recurrence check | 2
f capa_ref | CAPA | record | *
f recurrence_found | Recurrence found | boolean | *
f recurrence_records | Recurrence records | longtext | when=recurrence_found=true
f side_effects | New problems introduced | longtext
f reopen_investigation | Reopen the investigation | calc | {IF(OR(recurrence_found, effective_result = "Not effective"), "Yes", "No")}
sign eff_reviewed | Reviewed by | reviewed | I reviewed the effectiveness data recorded.
sign eff_approved | Approved by | approved | I approve the effectiveness decision. | capa.approve
end

template capa-closure | CAPA Closure | CAPA
packs medical-device, manufacturing
tags CAPA, closure
purpose Close a CAPA once its actions are implemented and effective, and confirm that documents, training, risk files and related records were updated.
scope All CAPAs.
instructions Confirm each closure condition. A CAPA closed as not effective must reference the new CAPA raised. Closure is approved by a person other than the CAPA owner.
workflow Closure requested, conditions checked, closure approved.
retention Keep for ten years after closure.
status Draft; Closure requested; Closed effective; Closed not effective; Reopened
section closure_checks | Closure conditions | 2
f capa_ref | CAPA | record | *
f all_actions_done | All actions implemented and verified | boolean | *
f effectiveness_done | Effectiveness reviewed | boolean | *
f docs_updated | Documents updated | boolean
f training_done | Training completed | boolean
f risk_updated | Risk assessment updated | boolean
f customer_informed | Customer informed of closure | boolean
f closure_outcome | Outcome | choice | * [Effective; Not effective - new CAPA raised]
f new_capa | New CAPA | record | reqwhen=closure_outcome=Not_effective_-_new_CAPA_raised when=closure_outcome=Not_effective_-_new_CAPA_raised
f closure_summary_text | Closure summary | longtext | *
sign closure_requested | Closure requested by | prepared | I confirm the closure conditions recorded.
sign closure_approved | Closure approved by | approved | I approve closure of this CAPA. | capa.approve
end
